    "answer": {
      "short": "$(12,\\ 15,\\ 18,\\ 21,\\ 25)$",
      "worked": "There are $11$ values, so the median is the sixth value. Excluding it, the lower half is $12,13,15,15,16$ and the upper half is $19,21,21,22,25$.\n$$\\begin{align*}Q_1&=15\\\\Q_2&=18\\\\Q_3&=21\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum is $12$ and the maximum is $25$. Draw the box from $15$ to $21$, the median at $18$, and whiskers to $12$ and $25$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": [
        {
          "id": "v2-8d6b9-p13-practice-slot-2-s2-q-solution",
          "role": "solution",
          "format": "tikz",
          "code": "\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=1cm,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\path[use as bounding box] (9.4,-0.65) rectangle (27.2,1.9);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (10,0)--(26.5,0);\n\\foreach \\v in {10,11,...,26}{\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\v,-0.09)--(\\v,0.09);}\n\\foreach \\v in {10,12,...,26}{\\node[below,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (\\v,-0.12) {$\\v$};}\n\\node[right] at (26.5,0) {$x$};\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (12,0.9)--(15,0.9) (21,0.9)--(25,0.9);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (12,0.5)--(12,1.3) (25,0.5)--(25,1.3);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (15,0.2) rectangle (21,1.6);\n\\fill[black] (17.96,0.2) rectangle (18.04,1.6);\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
